    {
      "id": "SHT-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-permutation-homology-order",
      "title": "The orbit and stabilizer bound on the order of permutation-module homology",
      "statement": "For j>0, a finite group S of order h satisfies |H_j(S,ℤ)|≤h^(h^j). For a G-set X with at most A orbits and stabilizer orders at most s≥1, |H_j(G,ℤ[X])|≤s^(A·s^j).",
      "hypotheses": "All stabilizers are finite. A and s are integer bounds. The number of elements in each orbit, and the order of G itself, may be infinite. Empty X gives the group of order one.",
      "correspondence": "The rank bound uses all inhomogeneous bar tuples. Annihilation by h gives a surjection from the residues of the coefficients of a free cycle basis onto the homology. The text splits by orbit; the archive bounds the same product inductively by removing a single orbit and using the long exact sequence. The resolution of C₂ checks the first two degrees separately.",
      "dependencies": [
        "SHT-01"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-stabilizer-order-bound"
      ],
