    {
      "id": "SHT-03",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-torsion-degree-shift",
      "title": "The degree shift from stabilizer homology to torsion of the augmented module",
      "statement": "Write K=ker(C₀→M) and C_p=ℤ[X_p]. For j≥1, the positive-degree segment of the long exact homology sequence gives |tors H_j(G,M)|≤s^(A s^j)·|tors H_(j−1)(G,K)|. Iteration with the degree-zero presentation gives b^A s^(j A s^j).",
      "hypotheses": "The equivariant complex is exact at M and C₀,…,C_j, with X₀,…,X_j having at most A orbits and stabilizers of order at most s≥1. For the iterated bound the ℓ¹ length of every basis boundary C_(j+1)→C_j is at most b≥1. The finite torsion on the right follows by induction on homological degree for the shortened complex, starting with the degree-zero presentation.",
      "correspondence": "The source takes K as the image of the first boundary, then uses its injection into C₀ and the surjection from C₁. It takes the second of the two long exact segments to bound middle torsion by the full order on the left times the right torsion order. Iterating the sharper per-step factors gives the displayed uniform estimate, which the source absorbs at each induction step.",
      "dependencies": [
        "SHT-02",
        "HOM-01"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-torsion-shift-bound"
      ],
